cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
title: >-
  hDOM-toolkit: single-molecule genome mapping, structural-variant confidence, and SEM contour measurement
version: 1.0.0
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Three tools from a single study of single-molecule genome mapping. hdom assigns molecules to
  chromosomal loci from two-channel optical maps, re-ranking candidates by a windowed backbone
  correlation multiplied by a label-set F1. sv_confidence decides whether an inversion or
  translocation in one molecule is supported, importing hdom's scoring engine rather than
  reimplementing it. sem_length traces and measures DNA contours in SEM images. The aligner
  maligner (Mendelowitz et al., GPL v3) is bundled so the pipelines run without a separate build.
  Includes a two-chromosome example that runs anywhere and a genome-wide example against all 47
  HG002 chromosome maps, which are deposited as their own record (doi:10.5281/zenodo.22929196).
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      DOM: Dual Optical Mapping Integrating Sequence-Specific Barcodes and A/T Density Profiles
    journal: Small Methods
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.1002/smtd.70883
    notes: >-
      The dual-channel mapping method this software implements, including the cc_rg2 = cc_r *
      cc_g^2 candidate score. Please cite alongside the software.
    authors:
      - family-names: Jo
        given-names: Kyubong
  - type: dataset
    title: >-
      hDOM and SGM reference maps for HG002 v1.2 (Nb.BssSI)
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22929196
    notes: >-
      Required by the genome-wide example. 47 chromosome maps and the in silico Nb.BssSI
      restriction map, deposited separately because they are data derived from a public assembly
      rather than part of the program.
    authors:
      - family-names: Jo
        given-names: Kyubong
